<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The Hill approximation follows the same assumptions as the CR3BP which are below:</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Mass of Body 3 is negligible (m = 0)</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Body 1 and Body 2 are point masses</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Orbit is considered circular for Body 2 around Body 1 (time rate of change of omega is zero)</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In the hill approximation, the frame is centered on Body 2</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Hill approximation also assumes the distance between Body 1 and Body 2 is much larger than that of Body 2 and the small body</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
